#v(0.3cm)
*In git:* scripts, `typst/main.typ`, notes and folder skeletons. *Not in git:* everything in
`data/`, everything R generates, `_tinytrail.yaml` and all PDFs. A collaborator clones the
repo and re-runs the scripts to regenerate the rest.

= How to run

```sh
Rscript scripts/occupation_clean.R            # only when the cleaning changes
Rscript scripts/occupation_analyse_wages.R    # each time the analysis changes
typst watch --root . typst/main.typ                    # recompiles on every save
```

Scripts use `here()`, so they work from any working directory inside the project.
Run `typst` from the project root: `--root .` is what lets `main.typ` read `output/`
(Typst refuses files outside its root, which defaults to the folder of `main.typ`).
In `main.typ`, paths starting with `/` are relative to that root: `"/output/plots/"`.

= Conventions

*Script names:* `{dataset}_{role}.R`, with no numbered prefixes (`01_`, `02_`), because
the order always changes anyway. Running clean before analyse is the only rule.

*Function names* in `functions.R`: `f_` plus a category prefix, e.g. `f_plot_age_dist()`.

#grid(
  columns: (auto, 1fr, auto, 1fr),
  column-gutter: 8pt, row-gutter: 6pt,
  [`f_plot_`], [ggplot2 figures], [`f_calc_`], [derived statistics, transforms],
  [`f_tab_`], [tables (gt, tinytable …)], [`f_clean_`], [cleaning helpers],
  [`f_read_`], [custom data loaders], [], [],
)

*Intermediate data:* RDS by default, because it keeps factors, dates and labels.
Use CSV only if the clean data must be readable outside R.

= Adding a new dataset

+ Put the original file(s) in `data/raw/{dataset}/` or `data/raw/`.
+ Create `scripts/{dataset}_clean.R`: `source(here("scripts/functions.R"))`, read raw,
  clean, `saveRDS(…, here("data/clean/{dataset}.rds"))`.
+ Create `scripts/{dataset}_analyse_{topic}.R`: `readRDS()` the clean file, `ggsave()` to
  `output/plots/`, save tables to `output/tables/`, merge numbers into `output/data.json`
  under a `{dataset}` key.
+ Reference them in `main.typ`: `#image(plots + "…")`, `#include(tables + "…")`,
  `#data.{dataset}.n_total`.

= Requirements

R with `here`, `jsonlite`, `ggplot2`, `tinytable` and `tinytrail`
(`pak::pak("tinytrail-r/tinytrail")`). Typst for compiling.

